gression, reinforcing the importance of rigorous statistical evaluation. [Data: Entities (970); Relationships (1096)]\n\n## Method of Instrumental Variables\n\nThe method of instrumental variables is a vital technique used in multiple regression to address endogeneity issues, which can arise when independent variables are correlated with the error term. This method allows researchers to obtain consistent estimates of the regression coefficients by using instruments—variables that are correlated with the endogenous predictors but uncorrelated with the error term. The application of this method is crucial in econometric analysis, particularly in observational studies where controlled experiments are not feasible. By employing instrumental variables, researchers can improve the reliability of their findings and draw more accurate conclusions about causal relationships. [Data: Entities (3146); Relationships (3941)]"], "parameters": {"model": "nomic-embed-text"}}, "key": "embeddings_8a0d982b8d512ce238ca35b4068e520220233c0b63320b9b1577c3fb8e5e4e6a_v2"}